ENGLISH
============================================================================

OpenYTMusic's source code is published so anyone can READ it. That is all that
is permitted. In short: you may look, you may not take.

1. YOU ARE ALLOWED TO
   a) Read, study and learn from the source code in the public repository.
   b) Install and use the official application (the APK distributed by the
      author) on your own devices, free of charge and without time limits.
   c) Build it for yourself, on your own machines, for personal, non-commercial
      use (for example to test the project or audit its security).
   d) Quote short excerpts for review, teaching or criticism, with attribution.

2. YOU ARE NOT ALLOWED TO
   a) Copy, reuse or extract the code, in whole or in part (copy-paste, porting
      to another language, embedding it in another project, etc.).
   b) Modify it and publish it, or distribute modified versions (public forks,
      your own builds, republishing on stores or websites).
   c) Redistribute or sell it, or package it inside another product.
   d) Use it for commercial purposes, or to build (or train) a derivative
      product or service.
   e) Publish binaries of the project, or let a third party do so, in any form
      and by any means.
   f) Use the name "OpenYTMusic", its logo or its signature to endorse or
      promote anything without prior written permission.

   If you want to do anything from the list above, ask the author in writing.
   The answer may be yes, but it has to be an explicit yes.

3. THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE NOTICES
   This repository includes third-party modules and dependencies, each under its
   own license, which are respected as-is and are NOT covered by the terms
   above:
     - Material Color Utilities — Apache License 2.0
     - LrcLib, KuGou and the InnerTube client — per their original projects
     - Parts of the YouTube Music client derive from GPL-3.0 open source
       projects (for example, InnerTune). Each file or module keeps, where
       applicable, its original header and license.
   No authorship is claimed over those people's work: the credit is theirs, and
   their code is governed by their licenses, not by this one.

4. WARRANTY
   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
   IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
